# AQP IDE (Theia 1.72 + six AQP extensions)

`aqp_ide/` is the AQP IDE — a white-labeled Eclipse Theia 1.72
distribution plus **six** AQP compile-time extensions:

- `theia-extensions/aqp/` — Auth0 PKCE login + 5 operator widgets +
  9-endpoint kill-switch + tenancy QuickPick + `/aqp/config` endpoint
- `theia-extensions/aqp-shell/` — white-label theme + `FilterContribution`
  lockdown + window-title + About dialog
- `theia-extensions/aqp-mcp-bridge/` — pre-configures Theia AI MCP for
  `aqp-data-mcp` + `aqp-codebase-mcp` (AQP rule 49)
- `theia-extensions/aqp-research-copilot/` — Theia AI `ChatAgent` routed
  through `router_complete` (AQP rule 2)
- `theia-extensions/aqp-notebook-quant/` — FINOS Perspective MIME
  renderer for Arrow + `File → New AQP Notebook` scaffolder
- `theia-extensions/aqp-quant/` — SpecAuthor + RunInspector (rule 4) +
  BacktestRunner widgets

## Hard boundaries

1. AQP-specific behaviour lives ONLY inside `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp*/`.
   Do NOT sprinkle AQP imports into core Theia files.
2. Do NOT `import` from `agentic_quant_platform` source code (Python or
   TypeScript) into Theia extension TypeScript. Cross the boundary only
   through HTTP (`AqpApiService` from `theia-ide-aqp-ext`) or the
   DataMCP / CodebaseMCP HTTP surfaces.
3. The **canonical operator entrypoint** is `aqp-cli ide` (subcommands:
   `install`, `build`, `start`, `stop`, `status`, `logs`, `open`,
   `url`, `env`, `detect`, `doctor`). Production / Docker / K8s
   workflows MUST go through the CLI. Direct `yarn` invocations are
   inner-loop development only.
4. **LLM calls (AQP rule 2).** The `aqp-research-copilot-ext` is the
   only sanctioned LLM consumer in the IDE. It MUST go through
   `RouterCompleteClient` (`POST /llm/router/complete`). NEVER import
   `@theia/ai-anthropic`, `@theia/ai-openai`, `@theia/ai-ollama`,
   `@theia/ai-vercel-ai`, `@theia/ai-google` for the AQP agent — those
   bundled adapters belong to upstream Theia AI's generic agents.
5. **MCP audience (AQP rule 49).** Every MCP server registration in
   `aqp-mcp-bridge-ext` MUST mint a token with the per-MCP `aud` claim.
   The bridge sets a non-secret `X-AQP-MCP-Audience` header so
   operators can verify the wiring from browser devtools without
   inspecting the token. NO token passthrough across audiences.
6. **Canonical progress frame (AQP rule 4).** The `RunInspectorWidget`
   in `aqp-quant-ext` consumes `{task_id, stage, message, timestamp,
   **extras}` verbatim. New WebSocket subscribers added to the IDE MUST
   honour the same frame shape.
7. **Tenancy headers (AQP rule 51).** `AqpApiService` attaches
   `X-AQP-Workspace` / `X-AQP-Project` / `X-AQP-Lab` / `X-AQP-Org` /
   `X-AQP-Team` on every HTTP request. WebSocket subscriptions pass the
   same headers via query params (browsers can't set Authorization on
   WS handshakes). The MCP bridge re-registers servers on every
   tenancy change.
8. **No secret printing** (`.cursor/rules/aqp-management-engine.mdc`).
   The redacted 4-character prefix rule applies to every log line in
   every IDE extension. NEVER print a full Auth0 bearer.
9. Keep browser / electron target scope explicit in docs and commands.
   The browser app is the AQP-wired target; electron remains
   upstream-oriented unless explicitly added.
10. Validate script names against `aqp_ide/package.json` and
    `aqp_ide/applications/browser/package.json` before documenting
    them.
11. Reference AQP paths through `aqp_ide/docs/aqp-monorepo-paths.md`
    (in-folder) or `aqp_docs/aqp-monorepo-paths.md` (monorepo-wide).
    NEVER hardcode local absolute paths.

## Where changes go

| Change | Path |
| --- | --- |
| New AQP-specific widget | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp-quant/src/browser/widgets/` (or a NEW `theia-extensions/aqp-<name>/` if it doesn't fit the quant theme) |
| New MCP server registration | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp-mcp-bridge/src/browser/mcp/` + add the slot to `AqpRuntimeConfig.mcp` in `theia-extensions/aqp/src/common/aqp-protocol.ts` |
| New copilot prompt | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp-research-copilot/src/browser/copilot/prompts/<name>.md` + register in `AqpResearchAgent.prompts` |
| New copilot tool | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp-research-copilot/src/browser/copilot/aqp-tool-functions.ts` |
| New notebook MIME renderer | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp-notebook-quant/src/browser/notebook/<name>-renderer.ts` |
| New CLI subcommand | `aqp_cli/src/aqp_cli/commands/ide.py` |
| New env var | `aqp_ide/theia-extensions/aqp/src/common/aqp-protocol.ts` + `aqp-config-endpoint.ts` + `aqp_ide/browser.Dockerfile` + `aqp_platform/deployments/kubernetes/aqp-ide/configmap-aqp.yaml` + `_THEIA_ENV_KEYS` in `aqp_cli/src/aqp_cli/commands/ide.py` |
| New K8s manifest | `aqp_platform/deployments/kubernetes/aqp-ide/` (single-pod overlay) |
| New doc | `aqp_ide/docs/` + cross-link in `aqp_ide/docs/index.md` + `aqp_ide/AGENTS.md` |
| New skill | `aqp_ide/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` |

## Validation

```bash
# Production entrypoint:
aqp-cli ide doctor
aqp-cli ide install
aqp-cli ide build --dev
aqp-cli ide start --open

# Inner-loop dev:
cd aqp_ide
yarn install
yarn build:extensions
yarn build:applications:dev
```

Build / lint / typecheck of every extension MUST pass before merge.

